A Day Under the Harbour (海底下的一天): credits

An unofficial fan film. It is not made, endorsed or checked by the Transport Department, by any bus operator or by the
operators of the harbour tunnels. No operator's logo, livery, sign layout or chime is used; route numbers, destinations
and stop names are public facts, shown as the timetable publishes them.

Timetable: Transport Department, The Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region.
  "Headway information of public transport services" (GTFS), DATA.GOV.HK,
  https://data.gov.hk/en-data/dataset/hk-td-tis_11-pt-headway-en
  files https://static.data.gov.hk/td/pt-headway-tc/gtfs.zip and https://static.data.gov.hk/td/pt-headway-en/gtfs.zip,
  downloaded 2026-11-13 (files dated 2026-11-10). Terms: DATA.GOV.HK Terms and Conditions of Use,
  https://data.gov.hk/en/terms-and-conditions : free for commercial and non-commercial use, with the source identified,
  the Government's and the Transport Department's ownership of the intellectual property in the data acknowledged,
  and attribution to the Government, the Transport Department and DATA.GOV.HK. The data is provided "as is".
  Used: the bus trips of service day 2026-11-18 (Wednesday) and the night trips of 2026-11-19 before 05:00 that call on
  both Hong Kong Island and elsewhere, cut down by tools/prep.py into data/bus.json. Most trips in this feed are
  published as headways (one bus every N minutes in a period): neo/geo/gtfs.py expands them into one departure per
  headway, so the dots are where the published timetable puts a bus, not real vehicles. Stop times the feed leaves
  blank are interpolated by distance. Counts on screen are ours, made from this file (see FACTS.md).

Map data: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0. https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Fetched 2026-11-13 through the Overpass API: the coastline (neo/geo/osm.py), bus route relations (neo/geo/routes.py)
  and drivable roads (tools/roads.py), kept as raw answers in data/*.cache/ (not committed). The derived files
  data/bus.json (route paths) and data/map.json (coast) are a derived database and stay under ODbL 1.0. The film is a
  produced work: it credits OpenStreetMap on its last card.
  Paths: 244 of the 486 stop patterns follow the OSM bus route relation with the same number; the other 242 follow a
  shortest drivable route along OSM roads between consecutive published stops (tools/prep.py). Tunnels are assigned by
  where each path crosses the harbour.
  View: Hong Kong and the harbour only (113.82-114.44 E, 22.14-22.58 N at most; the widest frame shows about
  113.84-114.41 E, 22.22-22.45 N), north up. No national, provincial or other boundary line is fetched or drawn.

Tunnel opening years: Transport Department, "Tunnels and Bridges: Details and Location Maps",
  https://www.td.gov.hk/en/transport_in_hong_kong/tunnels_and_bridges_n/location_map/index.html (see FACTS.md).

Font (fetched by tools/fonts.sh into fonts/, not kept in git):
- Fusion Pixel Font (缝合像素字体), 12px proportional, zh_hk and zh_hans, release 2026.10.25. TakWolf.
  SIL Open Font License 1.1. https://github.com/TakWolf/fusion-pixel-font
  (It includes glyphs from Ark Pixel Font, Cubic 11 and Galmuri, all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.)

Picture: drawn entirely in code (a brightness buffer in JavaScript, the board shaded in WebGL2). No images, video or
3D models are used.
Sound: the score, every sound effect and the ambience are synthesized in mix.py with numpy. No samples or recordings.

Tools: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame
capture, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; NEO-Cine's neo/ tools (gtfs.py, routes.py, osm.py, cues.py, master.py,
remote.sh).

Form reference (grammar only; no layout, typeface, livery or sound is copied): bus destination signs and stop displays,
departure boards, LED walls.
